        "notes": "Watering conflict: NC State says keep the mix moist while growing, Clemson (general dracaena advice, not corn plant specific) says let it dry a little first. Kept the wetter one per rule 5, from_knowledge_verify; to be picked by a reviewer. Temperature is NC State (70 to 80 F), Clemson's general dracaena advice is 60 to 70 F. Size is the 'Massangeana' houseplant figure from Clemson (4 to 5 ft, 2 ft spread, upper values); NC State gives 3 to 14.5 ft. Severity 1 maps NC State low severity and ASPCA saponin signs. The UF/IFAS FP184 page redirected and was not fetched. Anchor: baseIntervalDays 10 -> 8 for a 3-litre reference pot, from measured water use (Dracaena fragrans 'Lemon Lime', 44.3 g a day); the conversion to days is our arithmetic (02i), so guess."
      },
